{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated OWL modeling patterns but fundamentally misunderstands EDIFACT D96A INVOIC structure. It conflates abstract business concepts with concrete EDIFACT segments, lacks qualifier-based distinctions (NAD+BY vs NAD+SU), and is missing ~70% of mandatory D96A INVOIC segments. The 'HeaderSection/DetailSection/SummarySection' abstraction does not map to EDIFACT's flat segment sequence with hierarchical groups.",
  "completeness_score": 0.25,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "UNH_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Message Header (UNH) is MANDATORY in all EDIFACT messages. Must include S009 composite (message identifier with 0065='INVOIC', 0052='D', 0054='96A', 0051='UN')."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name", "owl_reviewed_length": 22380, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 0}

